      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783513888030,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Facebook News Feed\nA product that shows recent stories, allows you to post, follow and view your followers feed.\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Facebook News Feed\nA product that shows recent stories, allows you to post, follow and view your followers feed.\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ZugDvYROCz3VUJP9mj-AB",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5089.680776236629,
      "y": 1268.3543345244043,
      "width": 946.6792602539062,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1544554503,
      "version": 579,
      "versionNonce": 809204295,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783514201432,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Functional Requirements\n- Create posts\n- Follow people\n- View feed (constructed from people they follow, in reverse chronological order i.e. newest first)\n- Page through feed (scroll down to load new feeds)\n\nNote : follow is uni-directional vs friend is bi-directional\n\nNon-functional Requirements\n- Posts visible in < 1 minute(eventual consistency i.e. availability >> consistency)\n- Posting and viewing posts < 500ms\n- Massive number of users 2B\n- Unlimited followers and follows",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Functional Requirements\n- Create posts\n- Follow people\n- View feed (constructed from people they follow, in reverse chronological order i.e. newest first)\n- Page through feed (scroll down to load new feeds)\n\nNote : follow is uni-directional vs friend is bi-directional\n\nNon-functional Requirements\n- Posts visible in < 1 minute(eventual consistency i.e. availability >> consistency)\n- Posting and viewing posts < 500ms\n- Massive number of users 2B\n- Unlimited followers and follows",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "w_TmQo-VYTY3BWDvXzzvs",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5076.894171876787,
      "y": 1653.919635221077,
      "width": 573.4395751953125,
      "height": 150,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1226088135,
      "version": 110,
      "versionNonce": 499668839,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783514251077,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Core Entities\n- Post\n- User\n- Follow\n\nFollow stores a uni-directional link b/w users in our system",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Core Entities\n- Post\n- User\n- Follow\n\nFollow stores a uni-directional link b/w users in our system",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "asF8XYSaQTtFAuFPcecyt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5071.388401429782,
      "y": 1894.5636829583887,
      "width": 1162.37939453125,
      "height": 650,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1549219625,
      "version": 839,
      "versionNonce": 255967401,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783515258011,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "APIs\n\n// create post\nPOST /posts\n{\n    \"content\": {}\n}  -> 201 Created {\n                            \"postId\": // ....\n                       }     <-- Response\n\n// following a user\nPUT /users/{id}/follow  -> 200 OK\n\n\n// view our feed and page through it\nGET /feed?pageSize={size}&cursor={timestamp?}\nResponse ->  {\n                    items: Post[],\n                    nextCursor: string\n                 }\n\n\n\nNote : User auth(JWT) in header, Using PUT we ensure its idempotent and doesn't fails if user click follow twice.\nSince feed required in chronological reverse order, used TS as cursor to represent the oldest post they've seen so far.\nSo, each page returns N posts older than the TS",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "APIs\n\n// create post\nPOST /posts\n{\n    \"content\": {}\n}  -> 201 Created {\n                            \"postId\": // ....\n                       }     <-- Response\n\n// following a user\nPUT /users/{id}/follow  -> 200 OK\n\n\n// view our feed and page through it\nGET /feed?pageSize={size}&cursor={timestamp?}\nResponse ->  {\n                    items: Post[],\n                    nextCursor: string\n                 }\n\n\n\nNote : User auth(JWT) in header, Using PUT we ensure its idempotent and doesn't fails if user click follow twice.\nSince feed required in chronological reverse order, used TS as cursor to represent the oldest post they've seen so far.\nSo, each page returns N posts older than the TS",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "H6chAS5qrHDty3ZTVGRxC",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5543.7649278584295,
      "y": 2724.062039194239,
      "width": 1537.5589599609375,
      "height": 725,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a5",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1482634569,
      "version": 2966,
      "versionNonce": 2100960167,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1783523610929,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Notes\n- DynamoDB will be our choice of DB could be Cassandra as well basically any wide column DB works but using key-value store\n- Following/Frending a person is a many-to-many relation and can be modelled through graph, could use triple store or Neo4j\n  But for our purposes we use key-value store and model the graph ourselves.\n    - Graph DBs are usually useful for complex query requirements, like stepping different nodes, capturing friends or your friends or creating an \n      embedding for a recommendation system etc.\n- We have a Follow table, userFollowing(Partition Key) this is me the user, userFollowed(Sort Key) this is the user I follow.\n- We also create a Follow GSI with the reverse relationship (userFollowed(PK), userFollowing(SK)), this allows us to look for all the followers of a given user.\n- This allows us to do following things:\n    - check if the user is following another user : query with both partition key and sort key(userFollowing:userFollowed), a simple lookup\n    - get all the users a given user is following: query Follow with partition key(userFollowing), its a range query\n    - get all the users who are following a given user: query GSI with its partition key(userFollowed), its a range query\n\n\nViewing feed of post from people they follow\n- First, get all the users who a given user is following\n- Next, get all the posts from those users\n- Finally, sort all those posts by time and return\n- Its a Posts table heavy lookup, and just Posts with id as PK is not gonna cut it, need to add GSI(creatorId(PK), createdAt(SK))\n- This allows to get posts for from a set of users in chronological order.\n\n\nUsers page through their feed\n- This is supporting an \"infinite scroll\" like experience.\n- To achieve this we need to know what they've already seen - Easy, get the timestamp of the oldest post they've looked at.\n- Since, users are viewing from newest to oldest, that one TS tells us where they've stopped and a great cursor for next set of posts.\n- We've GSI on Posts sorting posts by creation ts, use it to return posts older than the cursor.\n    - get all users who a given user is following, get all posts from those users that are older than input ts, and sort all those posts by time and return\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Notes\n- DynamoDB will be our choice of DB could be Cassandra as well basically any wide column DB works but using key-value store\n- Following/Frending a person is a many-to-many relation and can be modelled through graph, could use triple store or Neo4j\n  But for our purposes we use key-value store and model the graph ourselves.\n    - Graph DBs are usually useful for complex query requirements, like stepping different nodes, capturing friends or your friends or creating an \n      embedding for a recommendation system etc.\n- We have a Follow table, userFollowing(Partition Key) this is me the user, userFollowed(Sort Key) this is the user I follow.\n- We also create a Follow GSI with the reverse relationship (userFollowed(PK), userFollowing(SK)), this allows us to look for all the followers of a given user.\n- This allows us to do following things:\n    - check if the user is following another user : query with both partition key and sort key(userFollowing:userFollowed), a simple lookup\n    - get all the users a given user is following: query Follow with partition key(userFollowing), its a range query\n    - get all the users who are following a given user: query GSI with its partition key(userFollowed), its a range query\n\n\nViewing feed of post from people they follow\n- First, get all the users who a given user is following\n- Next, get all the posts from those users\n- Finally, sort all those posts by time and return\n- Its a Posts table heavy lookup, and just Posts with id as PK is not gonna cut it, need to add GSI(creatorId(PK), createdAt(SK))\n- This allows to get posts for from a set of users in chronological order.\n\n\nUsers page through their feed\n- This is supporting an \"infinite scroll\" like experience.\n- To achieve this we need to know what they've already seen - Easy, get the timestamp of the oldest post they've looked at.\n- Since, users are viewing from newest to oldest, that one TS tells us where they've stopped and a great cursor for next set of posts.\n- We've GSI on Posts sorting posts by creation ts, use it to return posts older than the cursor.\n    - get all users who a given user is following, get all posts from those users that are older than input ts, and sort all those posts by time and return\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "v5F6RG3HHaFBMWzaMwi24",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3737.2563080154023,
      "y": 2086.226387315984,
      "width": 149.73504753704594,
      "height": 34.53301691751902,
